.TH SYS_CLOCK 2
.SH NAME
sys_clock \- nanoseconds since boot (SYS_CLOCK)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "mk.h"

long sys_clock(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys_clock
returns the time since the kernel started, in nanoseconds: a clock that
only goes forward, for measuring durations and timeouts. It does not
change when the wall clock is set; the date and time of day come from
.BR sys_time (2).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Nanoseconds since boot. It cannot fail.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_time (2),
.BR sys_sleep (2),
.BR sys_info (2)
